tools.description:
FIND people, accounts or deals by filter: the lists, not one record. Pick `kind`, then filter and sort. Examples:
  • deals closing this month → { kind: 'deals', filters: { status: 'open', closing_within_days: 30 }, sort: 'close_date' }
  • deals most likely to win → { kind: 'deals', filters: { status: 'open' }, sort: 'win_probability' }
  • ICP-fit accounts gone quiet → { kind: 'accounts', filters: { icp_fit: true, last_activity_before: '30d' } }
  • accounts most likely to close → { kind: 'accounts', sort: 'win_chance' }
  • who at acme.com → { kind: 'people', filters: { account: 'acme.com' } }
  • do we have sarah@acme.com → { kind: 'people', filters: { email: 'sarah@acme.com' } }
FILTERS BY KIND (anything else is refused with the reason):
  people: stage, source, status, has_email, has_linkedin, email, linkedin_url, icp_fit, min_icp_score, last_activity_before/after, account, include_all (also cold leads; then only stage, email, has_email, icp_fit, min_icp_score, last_activity_*, account). Sorts: last_activity, last_activity_asc, icp_score, icp_score_asc, recently_added.
  accounts: stage, icp_fit, min_icp_score, owner, country, has_open_deal, last_activity_before/after, include_all (skip the list window). Sorts: last_activity, icp_score, pipeline_value, health, win_chance (only accounts with an open deal, max 50).
  deals: account, pipeline (id from the CRM), status (open|won|lost), stage, owner, closing_within_days, min_amount, implied. No text search. Sorts: last_activity, close_date, amount, win_probability.
Stages are canonical: identified, connected, interested, meeting_booked, discovery, demo, negotiation, closed_won, closed_lost, disqualified, churned. A deal with `implied` is an account with no CRM deal (id implied:<account_id>). Open one row with get_context { focus: <its id> } — that works for people, accounts and deals.
